# L §2.3 (round 10) `enter = qid "+" "[" key ... "]" [CUR | ID] ["priced" price] ["lives" lspan]`, price `last(px)`;
# L §5.10: holdings, "each thing stating its unit and its price input as it enters (`holdings + [w1] etf_units priced
# etf_price lives ...`)", "value = units x p"; a price that is a reading is read with its carry. w1 receives 4 etf on
# 2026-02-01; px is 250 PLN/etf at 2026-03-31 and 260 PLN/etf at 2026-04-30. h1 (2026-03-31): 4 x 250 = 1 000 PLN.
# h2 (2026-01-15): no units yet, so no position is priced: 0 PLN. h3 (2026-04-30): 4 x 260 = 1 040 PLN.
=== pr.tally
model pr
  tally 2
  on 2026-06-30
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "synthetic"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
unit etf "fund unit"

kind fund_buys: event certain
  leg units: etf

place market: outside lives 2026-01-01..

input px: num PLN/etf reading
input n: num etf
input day: date

move buy: fund_buys
  on day
  leg units from market to w1 amount n

ask h1: value(w1, 2026-03-31) in PLN law 2026-06-30
ask h2: value(w1, 2026-01-15) in PLN law 2026-06-30
ask h3: value(w1, 2026-04-30) in PLN law 2026-06-30

version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  holdings + [w1] etf priced last(px) lives 2026-01-01..
  n = 4 etf "own"
  day = 2026-02-01 "own"
  px = 250 PLN/etf at 2026-03-31 "kurs"
  px = 260 PLN/etf at 2026-04-30 "kurs"
=== expect
h1: 1 000 PLN
  unfulfilled: buy
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
h2: 0 PLN
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
h3: 1 040 PLN
  unfulfilled: buy
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-06-30
